spans.s:
a-, an-, negative prefix:
(1) prefixed to finite verbs, as rarely in Skt. (Renou 〔p. 175〕) but rather often in Pali (CPD s.v. 7); here not common: apaśyanti SP 〔324.2〕; anatikramāmo Mv 〔ii.80.8〕; anicchiyati (?) Mv 〔iii.295.18〕; see 〔§ 23.17〕;
(2) in sense described for Pali in CPD s.v. 2, a cpd. in a- following the same word without a-, and preceding a form of kṛ: samitim asamitiṃ kṛtvā Divy 〔41.10〕, lit. making the assembly no assembly, i.e. quitting the assembly; tasya vacanam avacanaṃ kṛtvā Divy 〔41.28〕, disregarding his advice. See an-a-.
